addContext: the name the client sends
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
addContext: a wildcard
  server secureConnection: servername x.wild.test, alpn false, cert *.wild.test
  client secureConnect: cert *.wild.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
addContext: no context for the name
  server secureConnection: servername b.test, alpn false, cert localhost
  client secureConnect: cert localhost, alpn false
  client got "hello"
addContext: the last added that matches
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert *.test
  client secureConnect: cert *.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
addContext: a SecureContext
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
addContext: a client without SNI
  server secureConnection: servername false, alpn false, cert localhost
  client secureConnect: cert localhost, alpn false
  client got "hello"
SNICallback: a context for the name
  server SNICallback a.test, this is the socket true
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
SNICallback: later, a raw context
  server SNICallback y.wild.test
  server secureConnection: servername y.wild.test, alpn false, cert *.wild.test
  client secureConnect: cert *.wild.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
SNICallback: no context
  server SNICallback b.test
  server secureConnection: servername b.test, alpn false, cert localhost
  client secureConnect: cert localhost, alpn false
  client got "hello"
SNICallback: an error
  server SNICallback b.test
  server tlsClientError no certificate for that name, destroyed true
  client error ECONNRESET | Client network socket disconnected before secure TLS connection was established
  client got ""
SNICallback: a client without SNI
  server secureConnection: servername false, alpn false, cert localhost
  client secureConnect: cert localhost, alpn false
  client got "hello"
SNICallback over addContext
  server SNICallback a.test
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert *.wild.test
  client secureConnect: cert *.wild.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
ALPNCallback: its choice
  server ALPNCallback {"servername":"localhost","protocols":["x-a","x-b","x-c"]}
  server secureConnection: servername localhost, alpn x-b, cert localhost
  client secureConnect: cert localhost, alpn x-b
  client got "hello"
ALPNCallback: none of them
  server ALPNCallback {"servername":false,"protocols":["x-a"]}
  server tlsClientError ERR_SSL_NO_APPLICATION_PROTOCOL | SSL routines | no application protocol, destroyed true
  client error ERR_SSL_TLSV1_ALERT_NO_APPLICATION_PROTOCOL | SSL routines | tlsv1 alert no application protocol
  client got ""
ALPNCallback: one the client did not offer
  server ALPNCallback {"servername":false,"protocols":["x-a","x-b"]}
  server tlsClientError ERR_TLS_ALPN_CALLBACK_INVALID_RESULT | ALPN callback returned a value (x-z) that did not match any of the client's offered protocols (x-a, x-b), destroyed true
  client error ECONNRESET | Client network socket disconnected before secure TLS connection was established
  client got ""
ALPNCallback: it throws
  server ALPNCallback {"servername":false,"protocols":["x-a"]}
  server tlsClientError no protocol today, destroyed true
  client error ECONNRESET | Client network socket disconnected before secure TLS connection was established
  client got ""
ALPNCallback: a client without ALPN
  server secureConnection: servername false, alpn false, cert localhost
  client secureConnect: cert localhost, alpn false
  client got "hello"
ALPNCallback with ALPNProtocols
  createServer throws ERR_TLS_ALPN_CALLBACK_WITH_PROTOCOLS The ALPNCallback and ALPNProtocols TLS options are mutually exclusive
SNICallback and ALPNCallback
  server ALPNCallback {"servername":"a.test","protocols":["x-a","x-b"]}
  server SNICallback a.test
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn x-a, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn x-a
  client got "hello"
SNICallback without a certificate of its own, SNI
  server SNICallback a.test
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
SNICallback without a certificate of its own, no SNI
  server tlsClientError ERR_SSL_NO_SUITABLE_SIGNATURE_ALGORITHM | SSL routines | no suitable signature algorithm, destroyed true
  client error ERR_SSL_SSL/TLS_ALERT_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE | SSL routines | ssl/tls alert handshake failure
  client got ""
addContext, a key for another certificate: throws ERR_OSSL_X509_KEY_VALUES_MISMATCH error:05800074:x509 certificate routines::key values mismatch
requestCert: a context with the same ca checks the client certificate
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn false, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn false
  client got "hello"
requestCert: a context whose ca doesn't issue the client certificate refuses it
  server tlsClientError
  client got ""
addContext and ALPNProtocols
  server secureConnection: servername a.test, alpn h2, cert a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn h2
  client got "hello"
addContext and ALPNProtocols, none in common
  server tlsClientError ERR_SSL_NO_APPLICATION_PROTOCOL | SSL routines | no application protocol, destroyed true
  client error ERR_SSL_TLSV1_ALERT_NO_APPLICATION_PROTOCOL | SSL routines | tlsv1 alert no application protocol
  client got ""
https with SNICallback
  server request /a.test: servername a.test
  server request /localhost: servername localhost
  client a.test: 200, cert a.test
  client localhost: 200, cert localhost
new tls.TLSSocket(socket, { isServer: true, SNICallback })
  server SNICallback a.test
  server secure: servername a.test
  client secureConnect: cert a.test, alpn false
  client got "hello from a TLSSocket"
